<blockquote class="uncited"><div><blockquote class="uncited"><div>Hi !<br>Here is a recording where the audio bug (reception) can be heard. You can hear the wavering in my voice and the whispering.<br><br>Thanks !<br>73!</div></blockquote>Hi. I have exactly the same issue if I set the DMR Rx AGC to 3dB or more. The issue is stronger the higher the dB value is set. This applies to reception.The issue can be reproduced: while listening to a communication in progress on the repeater, go into Menu/Options/Sound Options and change the DMR Rx AGC: from off to 6 dB.<br>Often, simply entering the menu is sufficient. (but there must always be DMR Rx AGC increased)<br>On the home screen this also occurs but only sometimes.<br>RT3S SN 2202R03S11xxxxx STM CPU.<br>EDIT:I've just noticed that there may be a link to “Prompt: Beep”. When it is "Prompt: Silent" the problem does not seem to occur.</div></blockquote>Hi !<br><br>Yes, Same here. If I choose "Prompt: Silent". The problem is no more there. Same if I choose "DMR Rx AGC: Off".<br><br>Thanks !<p>Statistics: Posted by <a href="http://localhost/opengd77/memberlist.php?mode=viewprofile&amp;u=5359">ve2dka</a> — Tue Apr 22, 2025 3:03 am</p><hr />
]]></content>
